title: $:/plugins/rimir/namespace/examples/field-aliases
caption: field aliases

! Field aliases — alternative names on the target

Target-attached aliases live as a field on the target tiddler. No
separate index tiddler, no rewrite indirection — just a list of tokens
in a configurable field.

The field name defaults to `aliases` and can be changed via
[[$:/config/rimir/namespace/alias-field]]. The field value is parsed as
a TW title list so multi-word tokens use the `[[...]]` form.

!! Try it

This example uses the demo data tiddler
[[$:/plugins/rimir/namespace/examples/data/aliases/widget]]:

```
title:   data/aliases/widget
aliases: Widget [[The Widget]] OldName
```

With the ''Field aliases'' feature enabled, the following all resolve to
the same target:

* {{{ [[Widget]] }}} → <$let __nsref__="Widget" __nssrc__="$:/plugins/rimir/namespace/examples/field-aliases"><$link to={{{ [<__nsref__>ns-resolve<__nssrc__>] }}} class={{{ [<__nsref__>ns-resolve-class<__nssrc__>] }}}>Widget</$link></$let>
* {{{ [[The Widget]] }}} → <$let __nsref__="The Widget" __nssrc__="$:/plugins/rimir/namespace/examples/field-aliases"><$link to={{{ [<__nsref__>ns-resolve<__nssrc__>] }}} class={{{ [<__nsref__>ns-resolve-class<__nssrc__>] }}}>The Widget</$link></$let>
* {{{ [[OldName]] }}} → <$let __nsref__="OldName" __nssrc__="$:/plugins/rimir/namespace/examples/field-aliases"><$link to={{{ [<__nsref__>ns-resolve<__nssrc__>] }}} class={{{ [<__nsref__>ns-resolve-class<__nssrc__>] }}}>OldName</$link></$let>

!! Ambiguity

If two tiddlers declare the same token, the resolver refuses to pick a
winner. The link renders as unresolved with a `?` marker; hover for the
diagnostic listing the colliding tiddlers and the field to edit:

* {{{ [[Conflicting]] }}} → <$let __nsref__="Conflicting" __nssrc__="$:/plugins/rimir/namespace/examples/field-aliases"><$link to={{{ [<__nsref__>ns-resolve<__nssrc__>] }}} class={{{ [<__nsref__>ns-resolve-class<__nssrc__>] }}} tooltip={{{ [<__nsref__>ns-resolve-diag<__nssrc__>] }}}>Conflicting</$link></$let>

The two demo tiddlers that collide:

* [[$:/plugins/rimir/namespace/examples/data/aliases/widget-a]] — `aliases: Conflicting`
* [[$:/plugins/rimir/namespace/examples/data/aliases/widget-b]] — `aliases: Conflicting`

!! Locality narrowing (Restricted scope mode)

When //Scope// is set to //Restricted// in the settings tab with a
whitelisted prefix that contains one of the colliding tiddlers, the
resolver prefers the in-subtree pick. The link still works; the
tooltip surfaces the wider collision so users notice and clean up.

Try it: in [[settings|$:/plugins/rimir/namespace/settings]], switch
//Scope// to //Restricted// and add a prefix matching where you keep
your colliding tiddlers. Then re-render this tab — the `Conflicting`
link above will resolve cleanly (with a `·` marker and tooltip)
instead of going to the ambiguous state.

In //Global// scope mode (the default) no narrowing happens; any
collision is flagged as ambiguous.

!! Precedence

* ''Real tiddler beats alias'' — a tiddler with title `Widget` (if it
  existed) would still win over the field-alias.
* ''Field-alias beats NamespaceAlias rewrite-tiddler'' — target-attached
  declarations are closer to the truth than a separate rewrite.
* ''Walk-up does not participate'' — field-alias lookup is global, not
  contextual. The same `[[Widget]]` resolves the same way from
  every source (modulo Restricted-mode locality narrowing).
